  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tackling Serious and Organised Crime - Adam Smith International Ltd (ASI) Programme Delivery</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The programme will increase the capacity and commitment within government, civil society, and business to tackle Serious and Organised Crime (SOC). The programme focuses on key priority threats impacting the UK and Ghana: grand corruption, cyber-enabled crime, illicit financial flows (IFFs), narcotics and extractive, and organised immigration crime. It is designed to enhance the effectiveness of His Majesty&#x2019;s Government&#x2019;s (HMG) SOC operations by supporting the long term, institutional and political changes required for sustained improvement in the environment for combating SOC. The SOC-G programme focuses on Ghana, but recognising the transnational nature of these issues, it also looks to build better cooperation and partnership with Nigerian and UK agencies to deliver a trilateral institutional partnership to tackle SOC between these jurisdictions.</narrative>
  </description>
